I found out that the spellbooks have an interesting effect when read
out loud - it sends surrounding creatures to sleep! I continued my
efforts to escape the cell when the guard was dozing off: searching for
hidden doors, praying to Thoth (I sensed that he was displeased), and
quaffing my potions. For some reason one of them had ice cubes in it,
and it was shaped kind of like a horn, too! A frost horn? It was too
good to be true! I zapped it at the guard, but that only roused him and
give me a cryptic message about "Diet Pepsi".
     I tried on my rings, one of which was an engagement ring, the
other being a "Superman Decoder" ring. Unfortunately I didn't have
enlightenment so I couldn't tell what they were, and none of them did
anything useful for me. So eventually I just decided to n1000 it out.
     Finally some people came and took me away. I tried to resist, but
I didn't have a ring of free action and I couldn't escape from their
grasp. They stuffed me into the back of some sort of large container
and brought me to this new part of the dungeon called "Somerset Insane
Asylum", and quickly stuffed me into a small, padded room. They robbed
me of all of my possessions, and kicking the door down had no effect.
     Eventually I was let out and allowed to enter a room full of
books. Take that, Pakka Pakka! A free library! I immediately went
around trying to learn all the spells, but quickly found out that it
would take too many turns. Additionally, the guards here seemed to be
immune to the sleep effect of these weird books. I then chatted to the
other inmates, but the code strings for their replies seemed to be
corrupted. Desperate, I located a sink and quaffed from it, hoping to
get a bit of toxic waste. The water was always no good, but I didn't
worry as I didn't have any items. Still, for some reason, I must have
gained nutrition, because I felt bloated.
     I knew that this game couldn't get any worse, so when some @'s
came near me I attacked him, but my clumsy kicks did no damage. They
then force a cursed leather jacket on me - not only could I not take it
off, but my hands were tied behind my back! So I sat like this for a
very long number of turns, not even being able to clasp my hands
together to get a prayer to Thoth. My luck must have been very bad by
now, but eventually they removed the jacket from me somehow.
     They fed me food at regular intervals, which always consisted of
some bland ration and a potion. Most of the time it was fruit juice,
but occaisonally it was water, all of which I could stack together.
When they allowed me to wander around again, I dipped a spellbook into
one, and it didn't fade! So when I read it and I didn't suffer a
negative effect, I knew that they had been giving me holy water to
drink! I quickly stashed some of this with me.
